// Package sshkeys keeps the public keys of Git over SSH (people's keys and
// repositories' deploy keys) and the server's host keys, in the engine's
// database (tables ssh_keys and ssh_host_keys, schema 31), one code path for
// SQLite and PostgreSQL.
//
// A key's fingerprint is unique over every kind of key, so a key belongs to
// one owner: the person who added it, or the one repository it is a deploy
// key of. Host keys are generated by the first server to need them and
// sealed in the database, so every server that shares the database presents
// the same keys.
package sshkeys
